<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<dataModel xmlns="http://xmlns.oracle.com/oxp/xmlp" version="2.1"
           defaultDataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM">
  <!--
    DMT_WORKSCHEDULES_RECON_DM — BIP reconciliation report contract v1 for
    WorkSchedules (loaded via HCM Data Loader). Design doc: "BIP reconciliation
    report contract - v1" (nine columns, six parameters, keyset pagination) plus
    its HDL note: "each HDL object gets a Contract v1 report whose rows are the
    BASE tier (key + Fusion id); its ERROR rows are optional because HDL failures
    arrive per-record in the HDL response and are tagged [FUSION_ERROR] before the
    report runs."

    BASE-TIER ONLY. An HDL load has no interface table, so this report returns the
    BASE tier: one row per migrated record that Fusion positively confirmed by
    writing an HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP entry (SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER'),
    with the Fusion-assigned SURROGATE_ID as FUSION_ID. This is the same base-tier
    proof the Salaries, Absences and BenBeneficiary reconcilers use, and the design
    doc endorses it for HDL objects.

    ONE DMT OBJECT, TWO HDL BUSINESS OBJECTS (DMT_WORK_SCHED_HDL_GEN_PKG,
    2026-09-17 re-model). The generator writes one object zip carrying two .dat
    files, so this report returns a UNION of two OBJECT_TYPE branches — each Fusion
    HDL object reflected as its own row per the brief ("a work-schedule definition
    and its person-assignment may be separate OBJECT_NAMEs — reflect each as its
    own OBJECT_TYPE row"):

      (1) WorkPattern  — the pattern DEFINITION (+ its WorkPatternShift child).
          SourceSystemOwner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER'
          SourceSystemId    = (prefixed WORK_SCHEDULE_NAME) || '_WPAT'
          That _WPAT value is also the WorkSchedules TFM row's RECON_KEY (one key
          definition per object). On load Fusion records one
          HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP row per pattern:
            OBJECT_NAME='WorkPattern', SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER',
            SOURCE_SYSTEM_ID = our _WPAT key,
            SURROGATE_ID     = the Fusion-assigned base pattern id.

      (2) ScheduleAssignment — assign the schedule to a WORKER.
          SourceSystemOwner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER'
          SourceSystemId    = (prefixed PERSON_NUMBER) || '_WSASG'
          Base table PER_SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENTS.SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENT_ID is the Fusion
          id. HDL cannot create the Work Schedule wrapper (ZMM_SR_SCHEDULES; a UI
          task), so on a demo pod without that config the assignment side loads
          zero — honestly config-blocked — while branch (1) continues to prove
          patterns. This branch is present with the correct nine-column shape so it
          begins returning rows automatically once the wrapper config exists.

    BASE TABLE / FUSION_ID — HONEST NOTE (branch 1). Fusion assigns the WorkPattern
    a base id and records it as SURROGATE_ID in HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP. That
    surrogate is the authoritative, verifiable Fusion base id and is returned here
    as FUSION_ID. The pattern definition itself is visible to the FSCM BIP user
    through HTS_WORK_PATTERNS_VL (by WORK_PATTERN_NAME), which confirms every
    key-map row corresponds to a real, existing pattern (round-trip verified — see
    the PR body). Following the design doc's HDL note and the BenBeneficiary
    precedent, the key map (key + SURROGATE_ID) is the base-tier source of record.

    LIVE STATE ON THIS POD (verified 2026-09-20, fin_impl / ApplicationDB_FSCM):
      * WorkPattern:        11 HRC_SQLLOADER rows (our DMT loads, suffix _WPAT),
                            each SURROGATE_ID a real Fusion base pattern id.
      * WorkPatternShift:   22 HRC_SQLLOADER rows (children; not counted here — the
                            RECON_KEY is the pattern, one row per WorkSchedule).
      * ScheduleAssignment: 0 HRC_SQLLOADER rows (config-blocked as above; 556
                            FUSION-seeded rows exist and are never counted — the
                            SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER' filter excludes
                            Fusion-seeded rows).
      * Standalone rows + keyset paging (page -> advance -> empty) validated live;
        see the PR body for the exact rows.

    NINE response columns, in contract order:
      OBJECT_TYPE, RECORD_KEY, SOURCE_TYPE('BASE'), FUSION_STATUS('SUCCESS'),
      FUSION_ID (SURROGATE_ID / SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENT_ID), ERROR_MESSAGE (NULL),
      LOAD_REQUEST_ID (NULL), SOURCE_REF (= SourceSystemId), DMT_REFERENCE (NULL).
    SIX parameters: P_RUN_ID, P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID, P_IMPORT_ESS_ID, P_PREFIX,
      P_CHUNK_SIZE, P_AFTER_KEY.
    KEYSET pagination by RECORD_KEY (P_AFTER_KEY cursor, P_CHUNK_SIZE page).
      LOAD_REQUEST_ID / P_IMPORT_ESS_ID do not survive into the base for an HDL
      load, so BASE-tier matching is by run prefix (P_PREFIX). LOAD_REQUEST_ID is
      returned NULL per the brief's column mapping.
  -->
  <dataProperties>
    <property name="include_parameters" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_null_Element" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_rowsettag" value="false"/>
    <property name="xml_tag_case" value="upper"/>
  </dataProperties>
  <dataSets>
    <dataSet name="work_sched_recon" type="complex">
      <sql dataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM"><![CDATA[
SELECT
    object_type, record_key, source_type, fusion_status,
    fusion_id, error_message, load_request_id, source_ref, dmt_reference
FROM (
    -- Branch (1) WorkPattern (pattern DEFINITION). BASE tier: positive proof in
    -- the HCM integration key map. The HDL load writes one HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP
    -- row per pattern (OBJECT_NAME='WorkPattern',
    -- SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER') whose SURROGATE_ID is the Fusion base
    -- pattern id. One row per migrated work schedule (the _WPAT key == RECON_KEY).
    SELECT 'WorkSchedules'                AS object_type,
           m.source_system_id             AS record_key,
           'BASE'                         AS source_type,
           'SUCCESS'                      AS fusion_status,
           MAX(m.surrogate_id)            AS fusion_id,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS error_message,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(30))     AS load_request_id,
           m.source_system_id             AS source_ref,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS dmt_reference
    FROM   hrc_integration_key_map m
    WHERE  m.object_name         = 'WorkPattern'
    AND    m.source_system_owner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE '%\_WPAT' ESCAPE '\'
    GROUP BY m.source_system_id

    UNION ALL

    -- Branch (2) ScheduleAssignment (assign schedule to a WORKER). BASE tier:
    -- positive proof in PER_SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENTS, joined from the HDL key map
    -- (OBJECT_NAME='ScheduleAssignment', SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER',
    -- suffix _WSASG). Returns zero until the Work Schedule wrapper config exists
    -- on the pod; the join to the base table is present so real Fusion
    -- SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENT_ID values flow through as FUSION_ID once it does.
    SELECT 'WorkSchedules'                AS object_type,
           m.source_system_id             AS record_key,
           'BASE'                         AS source_type,
           'SUCCESS'                      AS fusion_status,
           MAX(sa.schedule_assignment_id) AS fusion_id,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS error_message,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(30))     AS load_request_id,
           m.source_system_id             AS source_ref,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS dmt_reference
    FROM   hrc_integration_key_map m
    JOIN   per_schedule_assignments sa
           ON sa.schedule_assignment_id = m.surrogate_id
    WHERE  m.object_name         = 'ScheduleAssignment'
    AND    m.source_system_owner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE '%\_WSASG' ESCAPE '\'
    GROUP BY m.source_system_id
)
-- Keyset predicate. An empty P_AFTER_KEY (first page) binds to NULL in BIP, so
-- treat NULL as "from the start": every non-null RECORD_KEY sorts after the empty
-- string. On later pages P_AFTER_KEY carries the previous page's last RECORD_KEY
-- and only greater keys are returned.
WHERE  (:P_AFTER_KEY IS NULL OR record_key > :P_AFTER_KEY)
ORDER BY record_key
FETCH FIRST :P_CHUNK_SIZE ROWS ONLY
      ]]></sql>
    </dataSet>
  </dataSets>
  <output rootName="DATA_DS" uniqueRowName="false">
    <nodeList name="data-structure">
      <dataStructure tagName="DATA_DS">
        <group name="G_1" label="G_1" source="work_sched_recon">
          <element name="OBJECT_TYPE"     value="OBJECT_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="OBJECT_TYPE"/>
          <element name="RECORD_KEY"      value="RECORD_KEY"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="RECORD_KEY"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_TYPE"     value="SOURCE_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_TYPE"/>
          <element name="FUSION_STATUS"   value="FUSION_STATUS"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="FUSION_STATUS"/>
          <element name="FUSION_ID"       value="FUSION_ID"       dataType="xsd:integer" tagName="FUSION_ID"/>
          <element name="ERROR_MESSAGE"   value="ERROR_MESSAGE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="ERROR_MESSAGE"/>
          <element name="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" value="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="LOAD_REQUEST_ID"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_REF"      value="SOURCE_REF"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_REF"/>
          <element name="DMT_REFERENCE"   value="DMT_REFERENCE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="DMT_REFERENCE"/>
        </group>
      </dataStructure>
    </nodeList>
  </output>
  <eventTriggers/>
  <lexicals/>
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="P_RUN_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_RUN_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_PREFIX" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_PREFIX" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <!-- Keyset pagination: page size + cursor. The reconciler calls with an empty
         P_AFTER_KEY first, then passes the last RECORD_KEY received on each next
         call, until a short page returns. -->
    <parameter name="P_CHUNK_SIZE" dataType="integer" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_CHUNK_SIZE" defaultValue="5000" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_AFTER_KEY" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_AFTER_KEY" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
  </parameters>
  <valueSets/>
  <bursting/>
</dataModel>
